{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778977462277,"sessionID":"ses_1ccb0b5deffelIFHYvg1Wda4b5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_beObpvqJdHEKeaSuz2SiZMp7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Updated `CL_0000135` from the outdated histology-style fibrocyte concept to `circulating fibrocyte`, revised the definition/comment to align with cited literature, added the requested narrow synonym `monocyte-derived fibrocyte`, and recorded the issue link in the term annotations.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Updated `CL_0000135` to represent the circulating blood fibrocyte concept requested in issue #3243.\n+\n+Summary of changes:\n+- Renamed the class label from `fibrocyte` to `circulating fibrocyte`.\n+- Replaced the old textual definition, which described an inactive fibroblast/histology concept, with a definition aligned to the circulating stromal cell concept discussed in the issue.\n+- Added a narrow synonym: `monocyte-derived fibrocyte`.\n+- Replaced the long free-text marker list comment with a shorter literature-backed summary describing coexpression of hematopoietic markers and collagen, migration to injury sites, and contribution to tissue repair/fibrosis.\n+- Added the issue tracking annotation linking the class to issue `#3243`.\n+- Updated the logical definition to include:\n+  - `stromal cell` as genus\n+  - `develops from` some `myeloid lineage restricted progenitor cell`\n+  - `capable of` some `antigen processing and presentation of peptide antigen via MHC class II`\n+  - `capable of` some `wound healing`\n+  - `capable of` some `positive regulation of angiogenesis`\n+- Removed the previous `develops from fibroblast` assertion because it conflicted with the revised circulating myeloid-origin concept.\n+\n+References used in the revised annotations:\n+- PMID:9177213\n+- PMID:20303382\n+- PMID:29286323\n+\n+Validation performed:\n+- Reviewed the existing `CL_0000135` axioms in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Checked referenced literature metadata/abstracts from PubMed for support of the circulating fibrocyte concept and its functional properties.\n+- Verified that the edited ontology file parses successfully with:\n+  - `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit.ofn`\n+\n+Completed checklist:\n+- [x] Read imported issue context\n+- [x] Inspected the existing term and related parent/progenitor terms\n+- [x] Updated text definition and label\n+- [x] Added requested synonym\n+- [x] Adjusted logical axioms to match the revised concept\n+- [x] Added issue tracking annotation\n+- [x] Validated syntax with ROBOT\n+- [x] Committed only the intended ontology file\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Updated `CL_0000135` from the outdated histology-style fibrocyte concept to `circulating fibrocyte`, revised the definition/comment to align with cited literature, added the requested narrow synonym `monocyte-derived fibrocyte`, and recorded the issue link in the term annotations.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@\n+Updated `CL_0000135` to represent the circulating blood fibrocyte concept requested in issue #3243.\n+\n+Summary of changes:\n+- Renamed the class label from `fi